meta {
  name: 72 EMI Panel Flow E2E
  seq: 72
}

script:pre-request {
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // EMI PANEL Flow E2E — folder-level setup (runs before every request here).
  //
  // Same shape as "71 EMI Machine Flow E2E", but the order carries a LAB PANEL
  // with THREE member tests instead of a single standalone test. This exercises
  // the panel path of the EMI endpoints AND the multi-parameter path: a panel is
  // one OrderItem (branchLabPanelId set, branchLabTestId NULL) whose member tests
  // live on the per-member LabReport rows as `memberBranchLabTestId` (the key the
  // adapter is mapped on). Two members are single-parameter tests (A: HGB, B: WBC)
  // and one is a MULTI-PARAMETER test (C: RBC + HCT + MCV on a single report).
  //
  //   bootstrap (siteadmin → tenant → branch → operator) →
  //   catalogue: THREE lab tests — A/B one result parameter each, C with THREE
  //     result parameters → import all three →
  //   build a PANEL of the three → import the panel into the branch →
  //   order the panel → accession bulk-collect + bulk-ACCEPT (creates one report
  //     per member test) →
  //   register the machine (siteadmin equipment + business lab adapter mapping
  //     ALL THREE member branch lab tests → token) →
  //   MACHINE scan (/emi/orders): ut_ids carry every member + every parameter from
  //     the single panel barcode → MACHINE submit (/emi/submitResult) with FIVE
  //     test_results entries fills all three member reports (three parameters on
  //     test C's one report) →
  //   verify every value landed (source = ADAPTER, status = SAVED), including all
  //     three parameters on the multi-parameter report.
  //
  // Every id/token is captured by each request's post-response via
  // bru.setVar(...) — nothing is copied by hand. Just Run Folder, or click Next.
  // A per-run unique id (panelRunId) keeps unique fields from colliding on re-runs
  // and is namespaced separately from flow 71 so both can run in one session.
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  if (!bru.getVar("baseUrl"))    bru.setVar("baseUrl", "http://localhost:3000/api/v1");
  // EMI endpoints live at the ROOT (not under /api/v1) — host only.
  if (!bru.getVar("emiBaseUrl")) bru.setVar("emiBaseUrl", "http://localhost:3000");

  // Entry point — the SEEDED platform SiteAdmin (prisma/seed.ts). The ONLY
  // credential this flow assumes exists; the tenant + business admin are created
  // at runtime. Change these two only if your seeded SiteAdmin differs.
  if (!bru.getVar("siteAdminEmail"))    bru.setVar("siteAdminEmail", "admin@kalnostics.com");
  if (!bru.getVar("siteAdminPassword")) bru.setVar("siteAdminPassword", "SuperSecret1");

  // Known passwords this flow sets (so every login is automated).
  if (!bru.getVar("operatorPassword"))       bru.setVar("operatorPassword", "Str0ng@Pass1");
  if (!bru.getVar("bootstrapAdminPassword")) bru.setVar("bootstrapAdminPassword", "Str0ng@Pass1");

  // TWO analytes — one per panel member test. Each `emiParamCode*` is sent as the
  // machine's `universal_test_id` and must equal the `parameterCode` created on
  // its member lab test (steps 14/15); each `emiParamName*` is that member's
  // `parameterName`, which appears in the scan's `ut_ids`.
  if (!bru.getVar("emiParamCodeA"))   bru.setVar("emiParamCodeA", "HGB");
  if (!bru.getVar("emiParamNameA"))   bru.setVar("emiParamNameA", "Hemoglobin");
  if (!bru.getVar("emiParamUnitA"))   bru.setVar("emiParamUnitA", "g/dL");
  if (!bru.getVar("emiResultValueA")) bru.setVar("emiResultValueA", "13.5");

  if (!bru.getVar("emiParamCodeB"))   bru.setVar("emiParamCodeB", "WBC");
  if (!bru.getVar("emiParamNameB"))   bru.setVar("emiParamNameB", "WBC Count");
  if (!bru.getVar("emiParamUnitB"))   bru.setVar("emiParamUnitB", "10^3/uL");
  if (!bru.getVar("emiResultValueB")) bru.setVar("emiResultValueB", "7.2");

  // Member test C is a MULTI-PARAMETER test: three analytes on ONE report. Each
  // `emiParamCodeC*` is sent as a `universal_test_id` and matches a `parameterCode`
  // created on test C (step 15c); `/emi/submitResult` fills all three onto the one
  // member report — the multi-parameter case this flow verifies.
  if (!bru.getVar("emiParamCodeC1"))   bru.setVar("emiParamCodeC1", "RBC");
  if (!bru.getVar("emiParamNameC1"))   bru.setVar("emiParamNameC1", "RBC Count");
  if (!bru.getVar("emiParamUnitC1"))   bru.setVar("emiParamUnitC1", "10^6/uL");
  if (!bru.getVar("emiResultValueC1")) bru.setVar("emiResultValueC1", "4.9");

  if (!bru.getVar("emiParamCodeC2"))   bru.setVar("emiParamCodeC2", "HCT");
  if (!bru.getVar("emiParamNameC2"))   bru.setVar("emiParamNameC2", "Hematocrit");
  if (!bru.getVar("emiParamUnitC2"))   bru.setVar("emiParamUnitC2", "%");
  if (!bru.getVar("emiResultValueC2")) bru.setVar("emiResultValueC2", "42");

  if (!bru.getVar("emiParamCodeC3"))   bru.setVar("emiParamCodeC3", "MCV");
  if (!bru.getVar("emiParamNameC3"))   bru.setVar("emiParamNameC3", "MCV");
  if (!bru.getVar("emiParamUnitC3"))   bru.setVar("emiParamUnitC3", "fL");
  if (!bru.getVar("emiResultValueC3")) bru.setVar("emiResultValueC3", "88");

  // Per-run unique suffix + derived mobiles (namespaced `panel*` so this flow
  // never clobbers flow 71's vars if both run in one session). Step 01's
  // pre-request FORCE-regenerates these at the start of every full-folder run, so
  // each run gets brand-new data (no re-run collisions / stale sample ids). This
  // guarded block is only a FALLBACK — it fires when a later request is run on its
  // own without step 01 having set the id first.
  if (!bru.getVar("panelRunId")) {
    const n = String(Date.now());
    bru.setVar("panelRunId", n.slice(-6));
    // 10-digit national mobiles (^\d{10}$) — distinct prefixes from flow 71.
    bru.setVar("panelAdminPhone",     "93" + n.slice(-8));
    bru.setVar("panelOperatorMobile", "92" + n.slice(-8));
    bru.setVar("panelPatientMobile",  "91" + n.slice(-8));
  }
}

docs {
  # EMI Panel Flow E2E — analyzer integration with a 3-test panel (incl. a multi-parameter test)

  A sibling of **71 EMI Machine Flow E2E**. It reproduces the exact same
  lab-analyzer round-trip (same `TOKEN` header, GET-with-`text/plain`-body, flat
  `{ s, m, … }` responses), but the order carries a **lab panel of three member
  tests** — two single-parameter (A: `HGB`, B: `WBC`) and one **multi-parameter**
  (C: `RBC` + `HCT` + `MCV`). It proves the EMI endpoints (a) resolve a scanned
  **panel** barcode down to its member tests, and (b) fill a **test that has
  multiple result parameters** — all its parameters onto that one member report.

  ## Why a panel is different
  A panel is stored as **one `OrderItem`** with `branchLabPanelId` set and
  `branchLabTestId = NULL`. Accession expands it into **one accession sample per
  member test**, and acceptance creates **one `LabReport` per member test**, each
  tagged with `memberBranchLabTestId` (a `BranchLabTest.id`). The adapter is
  mapped on those **member** branch lab tests — so `/emi/orders` must expand the
  panel and `/emi/submitResult` must fill each member report.

  ## How multiple parameters are handled
  For each member report, `/emi/submitResult` resolves **all** of the test's
  `LabTestResultParam`s and matches each independently against the machine's
  `test_results[]` (by `universal_test_id` / `test_name` / `display_name` →
  `parameterCode` / `parameterName`), writing one `LabReportResultValue` per
  matched parameter. So member test C's single report carries **three** analyte
  values from three `test_results[]` entries. (The test-name fallback that lets a
  machine send the *test* id instead of a parameter id applies only to
  single-parameter tests — a multi-parameter test must identify each parameter.)

  ## How to run
  Select this folder and **Run Folder**, or click **Next**. Each request captures
  the ids/tokens the next one needs via `bru.setVar(...)`. A `panelRunId` is
  generated once per run so re-runs never collide. The only credential assumed to
  exist is the **seeded SiteAdmin** (`admin@kalnostics.com` / `SuperSecret1`).

  ## Flow
  **Bootstrap:** 01 SiteAdmin login → 02 create tenant + business admin → 03
  business-admin login → 04 branch (enables all modules) → 05 operating schedule →
  06 operator user → 08 grant the operator collect + accept → 09 operator login.

  **Catalogue + panel:** 12 patient → 13 resolve branch master data → **14/15
  single-parameter tests A (`HGB`) and B (`WBC`)** → **15c multi-parameter test C
  (`RBC`+`HCT`+`MCV`)**, all created by the Business Admin WITH `resultParams` so
  each report is fillable → **16 import all three into the branch** (walk-in list)
  → 17/18/18c resolve `branchLabTestIdA` / `…IdB` / `…IdC` → **19 create a lab
  panel of the three tests** → **20 import the panel into the branch** (its members
  REUSE the branch lab tests imported in 16) → 21 resolve `branchLabPanelId`.

  **Order + accept:** 22 create the order with the **panel** as its single item →
  23 list accession samples (**three** samples — one per member — sharing **one
  barcode** under the default Dept+Sample grouping) → **24 bulk-collect** →
  **25 bulk-accept** (creates the three member `LabReport`s, PENDING).

  **Register the machine:** 26 SiteAdmin equipment → **27 lab adapter mapping ALL
  THREE member branch lab tests** → captures `flowAdapterToken`.

  **Machine talks to us:** **28 `GET /emi/orders`** — one scan of the panel
  barcode returns `ut_ids` carrying every member test name plus every parameter
  name (including C's three) → **29 `GET /emi/submitResult`** submits **five**
  analyte values (A, B, and C's three) in one call.

  **Logged (three scopes):** 30 branch / 31 business / 32 site-admin adapter-logs
  reads — the same as flow 71.

  **Verify every value filled:** 33 list the panel's reports (`?branchLabPanelId=`)
  — **three** reports, all `SAVED`, ids resolved by `memberBranchLabTestId` → 34/35
  the single-parameter reports A/B each carry their `ADAPTER` value (`13.5` / `7.2`)
  → **35c the multi-parameter report C carries all three** `ADAPTER` values
  (`4.9` / `42` / `88`) on one report.

  > Panel + multi-parameter counterpart of flow 71: **one panel barcode → every
  > member test AND every parameter in `ut_ids` → one submit fills all three member
  > reports, including three parameters on the multi-parameter report.**
}
